	"_comment": "Polski. Short passive participle register — exactly how Polish software phrases outcomes: 'Plik usunięty', 'Gałąź utworzona'. Agreement is one mechanical rule from the masculine base (-y → -a/-e: usunięty → usunięta/usunięte) and covers all 27 verbs here with no per-verb past_f overrides needed — every chosen participle happens to end in -y. Gerund slot is the imperfective verbal noun in -anie/-enie (Usuwanie..., Sprawdzanie...), the register real Polish installers/CLIs use; wypychanie (push) and znajdowanie (find) are the mechanically regular forms of the imperfective partners wypychać/znajdować — grammatically solid, though wysyłanie/wyszukiwanie are the more common everyday synonyms for those two concepts specifically. No articles (article.none). Nominative-only v1, accepted deliberately: real Polish wants the accusative object after a transitive verb, so 'Nie udało się wypchnąć gałąź' is grammatically a stand-in for 'wypchnąć gałąź' with the accusative (which for this feminine noun happens to look identical to the nominative — that coincidence is not to be read as case handling; no case declension is attempted anywhere in this file). Plural resolution is binary (one/other) per the engine's Pluralize(); Polish's own CLDR few/many split (2-4 vs 5+) is not modelled here — 'other' covers every count above 1, same simplification as the case caveat.",
